      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.52,
          "end": 4.68,
          "en": "-: We're nearing the end of the first part",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.68,
          "end": 7.95,
          "en": "of this section, the template-driven approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.95,
          "end": 10.05,
          "en": "There's still some things I want to show you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.05,
          "end": 12.9,
          "en": "For example, how to work with radio buttons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.9,
          "end": 14.61,
          "en": "We don't have any radio buttons",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.61,
          "end": 18.03,
          "en": "in our form as of now, so let's add some.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.03,
          "end": 20.31,
          "en": "Let's add a property in the app component first",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.31,
          "end": 21.63,
          "en": "with some genders.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.63,
          "end": 23.67,
          "en": "So this is simply an array where I have male",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 23.67,
          "end": 27.21,
          "en": "and female, and I don't want to insult anyone,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.21,
          "end": 29.4,
          "en": "I know there are more genders nowadays.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.4,
          "end": 31.53,
          "en": "I'm going to go with the classic approach here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 31.53,
          "end": 33.81,
          "en": "Just to keep it simple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 33.81,
          "end": 37.05,
          "en": "We have this genders array, and now with that array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 37.05,
          "end": 38.94,
          "en": "I want to output genders here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 38.94,
          "end": 43.89,
          "en": "So let's say below our, your reply paragraph here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 43.89,
          "end": 47.823,
          "en": "I'll add a new div with a class of radio.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.25,
          "end": 55.17,
          "en": "And this div should be replicated for all the genders.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.17,
          "end": 58.59,
          "en": "So I'm going to loop through my genders,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.59,
          "end": 61.32,
          "en": "maybe bind it to a gender variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.32,
          "end": 63.51,
          "en": "and this is just a set of bootstrap uses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.51,
          "end": 65.13,
          "en": "to give to give to some nice styling.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.13,
          "end": 67.08,
          "en": "Of course, use any other setup",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.08,
          "end": 70.83,
          "en": "to style your radio buttons here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.83,
          "end": 73.02,
          "en": "I'm looping through all the genders.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.02,
          "end": 75.3,
          "en": "And now again, in the bootstrap ball to make a,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75.3,
          "end": 77.19,
          "en": "to create a nice looking radio button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 77.19,
          "end": 79.05,
          "en": "I'm going to wrap it in a label.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 79.05,
          "end": 82.11,
          "en": "This input here, which is of type radio.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 82.11,
          "end": 85.23,
          "en": "And I'm going to wrap this over multiple lines too just",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 85.23,
          "end": 88.56,
          "en": "to make it all super simple to read and to understand.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 88.56,
          "end": 91.68,
          "en": "And here I will give it a name of gender because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 91.68,
          "end": 94.92,
          "en": "on a radio button, I can only select one of them in a group.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 94.92,
          "end": 97.11,
          "en": "So the name should be gender",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 97.11,
          "end": 99.69,
          "en": "for whichever button is selected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 99.69,
          "end": 103.89,
          "en": "And I will place ngModel on it to make it a control.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 103.89,
          "end": 106.44,
          "en": "And I will pre-populate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 106.44,
          "end": 111.24000000000001,
          "en": "or I will set the value of this button equal to gender.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 111.24000000000001,
          "end": 113.943,
          "en": "So this variable of my ng4 loop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 114.81,
          "end": 118.25999999999999,
          "en": "Now with that, if we save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 118.25999999999999,
          "end": 120.66,
          "en": "we should see that we have some gender buttons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 120.66,
          "end": 124.56,
          "en": "To output a text, I need to add it here after my input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 124.56,
          "end": 127.263,
          "en": "So again, gender here, like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 128.22,
          "end": 130.41,
          "en": "And now we have male and female here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 130.41,
          "end": 133.89,
          "en": "And if I just enter something so that I can submit the form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 133.89,
          "end": 136.44,
          "en": "and I pick male here, you will see that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 136.44,
          "end": 140.85,
          "en": "on the value object here we got gender,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 140.85,
          "end": 141.81,
          "en": "which is male.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 141.81,
          "end": 144.45,
          "en": "And of course, if I pick female, this will,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 144.45,
          "end": 147.36,
          "en": "you guessed it, be set to female.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 147.36,
          "end": 150.63,
          "en": "So this is how you can easily incorporate radio buttons",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 150.63,
          "end": 155.19,
          "en": "by binding or by placing ngModel on the input as always.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 155.19,
          "end": 156.57,
          "en": "Setting the value, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 156.57,
          "end": 158.85,
          "en": "you could also hard code the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 158.85,
          "end": 162.54,
          "en": "and that, well, makes it usable just like any other input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 162.54,
          "end": 165.96,
          "en": "And if you want to set it to a default gender, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 165.96,
          "end": 168.78,
          "en": "you can use one way binding again to make sure that one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 168.78,
          "end": 172.98,
          "en": "of the two buttons is selected by default at the start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 172.98,
          "end": 175.11,
          "en": "when you load the form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 175.11,
          "end": 179.673,
          "en": "You can also, of course, add the required directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 180.57,
          "end": 183.93,
          "en": "or attribute to that input here to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 183.93,
          "end": 186.84,
          "en": "that now the form will not be valid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 186.84,
          "end": 189.24,
          "en": "until one of the two has been selected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 189.24,
          "end": 191.58,
          "en": "So that works just like on any other input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 191.58,
          "end": 193.53,
          "en": "So I just wanted to highlight this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 193.53,
          "end": 197.43,
          "en": "because radio buttons can look like a very special case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 197.43,
          "end": 198.48,
          "en": "They aren't.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 198.48,
          "end": 200.82,
          "en": "They are used like any other input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 200.82,
          "end": 203.76,
          "en": "when using the template-driven approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 203.76,
          "end": 205.413,
          "en": "in your Angular app.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
